first round of a technical interview with LTIMindtree for a DevOps Engineer role (3–5 years experience level).
The discussion covered a wide range of real-time DevOps, Cloud, Terraform, Kubernetes, Jenkins, Docker, and Incident Management topics.
Some of the questions asked were:
• Tell me about yourself
• Explain your project architecture
• Why do you use EKS instead of ECS?
• Have you handled cloud cost or budget management?
• How do you set up monitoring tools like CloudWatch and Grafana?
• Write a Bash script to check disk usage and CPU usage
• Write a Terraform configuration to create an EC2 instance
• What would you do if the Terraform state file is corrupted?
• How do you handle infrastructure created outside Terraform?
• What steps do you take to prevent accidental infrastructure deletion?
• What do you do if a Jenkins pipeline fails?
• Difference between CMD and RUN in Docker
• How do you configure automatic Jenkins triggers from GitHub pushes?
• Explain deployment strategies used in your projects
• What actions do you take during a P1 incident?
• How do you prevent multiple associates from running Terraform simultaneously?
• How do you design a disaster recovery process for zero-downtime applications?
It was a great experience discussing practical DevOps scenarios and real-world production challenges. Sharing these questions here may help other DevOps engineers preparing for interviews.
